{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Peter at Work"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "And the Presentation Continues ..."}, {"type": "position", "content": 5}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 14}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe routines and regular activities in a wider range of social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Giving a Presentation"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "It is important to sound professional and prepared when giving a business presentation. You will also need to become familiar with the structure and vocabulary needed for a presentation. Below, you will find language you can use to give, structure, organize, link and finish off your presentation."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<ol start=1><li>Opening your presentation and introducing yourself</li></ol>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<ul><li>I'd like to welcome everyone to the meeting.</li><li>Thank you all for being here today.</li><li>Thank you all for making it at such short notice.</li><li>Shall we make a start?</li><li>Let's make a start.</li><li>My name is ... and I'm the ... for ... .</li></ul>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<ol start=2><li>Overview</li></ol>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<ul><li>We're here to discuss ...</li><li>The purpose of this presentation is to ...</li><li>The objective of this presentation is to ...</li><li>The main subject of this meeting is to ...</li><li>May I invite you to ask any questions at the end of the presentation? Thank you.</li></ul>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<ol start=3><li>Giving an Overview</li></ol>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<ul><li>Let me begin by presenting a short outline of my talk.</li><li><span class=\\\"underline\\\">First</span>, I will talk about ...</li><li><span class=\\\"underline\\\">Then</span> I'll outline a ...</li><li><span class=\\\"underline\\\">After that</span>, I will discuss ...</li><li><span class=\\\"underline\\\">Finally</span>, I will discuss ...</li></ul>(notice the adverbial linking phrases)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<ol start=4><li>Stating Important Points</li></ol>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<ul><li>There are a number of problems associated with ...</li><li>In the first place, / Firstly, ...</li><li>Secondly, ...  In contrast, ...</li><li>Another problem is ...  On the other hand, ...</li><li>Furthermore, ...</li><li>Another advantage is ... All in all, ... / In summary, ... </li></ul>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<ol start=5><li>Closing and Questions</li></ol>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<ul><li>OK then. To sum up ...</li><li>Right. In summary ...</li><li>Now the floor is open for questions ...</li><li>Now, if there are any questions ...</li></ul>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\"\"}"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Talking About What is Acceptable or Unacceptable"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "In the business world, there's a close connection between culture and social behavior."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Different cultures have different patterns of social behavior. What might be acceptable in some cultures may be perceived as being acceptable or unacceptable in other cultures. Here are patterns you can use to talk about what is acceptable or unacceptable."}, {"type": "example", "content": "North Americans are expected to be on time."}, {"type": "example", "content": "It is inappropriate for South Americans not to express their feelings."}, {"type": "example", "content": "South Americans usually express their feelings more openly."}, {"type": "example", "content": "North Americans consider it inappropriate to be late for a meeting."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Emotional speakers are considered unreliable."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Feelings are not expressed during meetings."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "rational"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "based on reasons rather than emotions"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: North Americans are expected to present their idea is a formal and rational manner."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le14ob05aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to discuss cultural differences."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "unreliable"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "cannot be trusted or depended on"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Emotional speakers may be considered unreliable."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le14ob05aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "dishonest"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "not honest, deceiving or cheating people"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: At a business meeting, emotional speakers may be considered dishonest or unreliable."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le14ob05aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "in contrast"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the opposite; compared to something else"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: In contrast to Americans, South Americans may express their feelings more freely."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le14ob05aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "dismissive"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "not paying attention to; ignoring"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: In the Latin culture, being dismissive is considered offensive."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le14ob05aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "whereas"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "used to compare two facts"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(conjunction)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It is acceptable in the U.S. for colleagues to disagree with one another, whereas a Latino may agree with their colleague."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le14ob05aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "offensive"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "very rude or insulting and likely to upset people"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Asking them questions like that may be offensive."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le14ob05aud07"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "in summary"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a short statement that gives only the main points of something, not the details"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: In summary, it is important to understand cultural differences and expectations to prevent misunderstanding."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le14ob05aud08"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to prevent"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to stop something from happening"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Open communication prevents misunderstanding."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le14ob05aud09"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "the floor is open"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to open discussion to everyone"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Thank you for listening. Now, the floor is open for questions."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le14ob05aud10"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn6le14ob05re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Think of a process you might like to change in your workplace or school. Why do you think it needs to be changed?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a short presentation of what process needs to be changed and how you'd like to change it."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make your presentation about 70 - 80 words. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Be sure to use the language necessary for a presentation."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Proofread your presentation."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read your presentation aloud to a partner. "}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I understand and use language necessary for a presentation."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write a short presentation about something I would like to change."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I deliver  my presentation to a partner. "}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "img_path": "", "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "id": 0, "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can give a presentation."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about what is acceptable and unacceptable."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about  appropriate behavior for jobs and work."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " Do you like listening to presentations? Why or why not?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " What was the last presentation you listened to? What did you think of it?"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "conte